 "note": "The strokes of tests/gpu_matrix.py: each names its tool by its button's data-tool (paint, erase, light), which stays when a label or a key changes; x and y from 0 to 1 on the frame, as ui_live.py's --strokes and --fluid. A colour is one of the page's swatches. A case's « seed » is the page's ?seed=: its first edit and its fluid shot start from it, each next edit from the next number, so a case paints the same strokes from the same seeds at every run. horse_erase's seed is a hard one for an erase with no words: at it, Klein's prompt writer can name the horse instead of the barn. A case with « like » takes another case's strokes and its seed, its brush multiplied by « scale ». The places on horse.mp4 were set on its first frame: the camera pans right, so what stands behind the fence slides left and passes behind the horse. horse_erase_barn is horse_erase with its object named, « the barn »; it is outside quick and all. horse_saddle (a blanket painted on the horse's back) and horse_bird (a crow on the right fence post that sits still, then flies away) are recordings of the follow matte (PAINTAPLATE_RECORD), outside quick and all too. hdr_cow paints horse_cow's strokes from its seed on the HDR test plate (tests/hdr_plate.py makes it from horse.mp4 when it is missing), with SDR to HDR on, so the report gives HDR Match's line; it is outside quick and all. tos_arm paints a robotic arm over the raised forearm of shot 05_4a of Tears of Steel (CC BY 3.0) and over everything strapped on it, in one wide stroke whose words say what each strapped part becomes: its 121 EXR frames, 480 to 600 of https://media.xiph.org/tearsofsteel/tearsofsteel-footage-exr/05_4a/linear_hd/, in input/plates/tos_05_4a, with SDR to HDR on. Its stage_frames draw stages.png, and it is outside quick and all. car_trees cleans the car of plates/1280p_car.mp4 with no words, then paints « Trees growing on the road » in two upright strokes: the points of a stroke can hold several paths, drawn in turn before Generate, for one edit. Its « stage_frames », in the plate's own frame numbers, draw stages.png: those frames of the plate, of the Clean matte (the hole the clean plate pass fills) and of each full-size stage, the clean plate pass, the shot, the paint matte and the composite. It is outside quick and all. car_trees_shadow is car_trees with the Clean painted as is over the car and its cast shadow (« whole » off): the same Paint, the same seed. It is outside quick and all. The MP4 plates of plates/ are on the Hugging Face dataset AInVFX/ainvfx-paintaplate (CC BY 4.0): get_plates.py downloads every one into input/plates of the ComfyUI the pack is in. plates/horse_hdr comes from tests/hdr_plate.py, plates/tos_05_4a from tests/tos_plate.py. tos_arm_clean cleans the rig strapped on that forearm, named part by part for SAM 3.1, then paints a robotic arm on the same points with a narrower brush and shorter words. It is outside quick and all, and its stage_frames draw stages.png. A case's « address » adds options to the page's address, and « beside » names a case whose export, run into the same folder, sits beside its own on the sheet. It is outside quick and all. horse_erase's stage_frames draw stages.png at frames 101, 111 and 121. horse_cow_4k and horse_erase_4k are horse_cow and horse_erase with Finish > Upscale on (« upscale »): Export then writes the upscaled set too, and the zip holds it under upscaled/ (the result, the plate, the layer and the matte at 3840 x 2160). They are outside quick and all. horse_laser paints two red laser beams from the horse's head, one towards the frame's right edge and one towards its bottom, in two strokes of one edit: the beams keep their place over the first frames, then turn as the horse turns its head. It is outside quick and all. horse_smoke paints thin light grey smoke rising from the barn's roof, in one stroke: a soft paint, faint at its edges. It is outside quick and all.",
