 "tos_arm": {"path": "plates/tos_05_4a", "seed": 139, "hdr": true, "stage_frames": [480, 520, 560, 600], "strokes": [["paint", "Turn the raised forearm and hand into a robotic arm, in place of the arm and of everything strapped on it. The hand and the forearm become dark brushed-metal segments with visible joints and small actuators at the wrist. The grey tape straps become bundles of thin coloured wires and black cables that run along the forearm; the loose strap ends that hang below the arm become hanging cables. The black plate becomes a machined metal rail bolted on the forearm. The four black rods stay where they are and become thin metal antennas; each orange tip becomes a small, very bright white LED. The red ball at the wrist becomes a red signal lamp. A row of very bright blue-white LEDs shines along the wiring of the forearm and lights the metal around it. The robotic arm keeps the exact position, size, angle and outline of the original arm. Keep the blurred head on the left, the blue sleeve, the blurred street behind, the soft daylight, the depth of field, the framing and the composition exactly as they are.", [[0.42, 0.45], [0.48, 0.55], [0.55, 0.66], [0.62, 0.77], [0.68, 0.87]], 160, {"color": "#000000"}]]},
